      "id": "540",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 540,
        "relationship_type": "synonym",
        "body": "Both express potential or ability, like 'can do'. ことができる is more formal and common in writing, e.g. 書くことができる 'can write', while the potential form れる・られる is shorter and used in conversation, e.g. 書ける 'can write'. The meaning is the same, but usage differs by tone and context.",
